    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a6ef2dd1-218d-5e1e-8319-79d4ecb1570f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eleutherococcus, Amaryllis, Chengiopanax sciadophylloides, Hippeastrum puniceum\n- Taxonomy: Araliaceae, Amaryllidinae, Amaryllideae, genus classification, ITS sequence data\n\nFacts:\n- Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\n- Amaryllis is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae within the tribe Amaryllideae.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides was previously included in the genus Eleutherococcus.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides is distinguished from Eleutherococcus because it does not have spines or prickles.\n- ITS sequence data confirmed the separation of Chengiopanax sciadophylloides from Eleutherococcus.\n- Hippeastrum puniceum has common names including Barbados lily, Easter lily, cacao lily, cocoa lily, and amaryllis lily.\n- Hippeastrum puniceum is neither a lily nor a species of Amaryllis.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6d448fe5-6862-575c-b174-add5d2892379",
        "text": "Page: Eleutherococcus. Sentence: Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\nPage: Amaryllis. Sentence: Amaryllis ( ) is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae (tribe Amaryllideae).\nPage: Chengiopanax sciadophylloides. Sentence: Previously included in the genus \"Eleutherococcus\", it is distinguished from other members of that genus by not having spines or prickles and ITS sequence data confirmed the separation.\nPage: Hippeastrum puniceum. Sentence: Common names include Barbados lily, Easter lily, cacao lily, cocoa lily and amaryllis lily, although it is neither a lily nor a species of \"Amaryllis\".",
